Terraform Core Commands:
terraform init
Initializes the Terraform project by downloading providers and setting up state.

terraform plan
Shows what changes Terraform will make before applying them.

terraform apply
Creates or updates infrastructure based on the Terraform files.

terraform destroy
Deletes all infrastructure managed by Terraform.


terraform init     → setup Terraform
terraform plan     → preview changes
terraform apply    → create/update infra
terraform destroy  → remove infra


RPC (Remote Procedure Call)
Used by Terraform to communicate with provider plugins.

Terraform sends requests to providers using RPC, and providers perform actions on cloud resources.

RPC → Terraform talks to cloud providers via plugins

Terraform CLI
     │
     ▼
Provider Plugin (RPC)
     │
     ▼
Cloud Provider API
     │
     ▼
Infrastructure (EC2, VPC, S3, etc.)
Terraform uses RPC to talk to provider plugins, which call cloud APIs to manage infrastructure.

